From: summit <summit@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: do not crash in shutdown if not bound

If display subcomponents fail to probe, probe is deferred, or the device
is a secondary MMSYS instance, private or private->drm may be NULL, and
private->drm_master may be false. Calling drm_atomic_helper_shutdown()
under these conditions causes a NULL pointer dereference.

Add checks to ensure mtk_drm_shutdown() only runs on the bound master
DRM device with a valid drm pointer.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
index 37d8113..69a4c52 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
@@ -1348,6 +1348,9 @@ static void mtk_drm_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct mtk_drm_private *private = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
+	if (!private || !private->drm_master || !private->drm)
+		return;
+
 	drm_atomic_helper_shutdown(private->drm);
 }
 
